          "Analyse informal disposal in terms of the actual controls that could be lost. An unidentified scrap buyer may provide no reliable onward destination, no reconciliation of missing assets and no assurance about batteries or confidential media. The initial cash offer can therefore conceal investigation work, replacement documentation costs, safety exposure and a loss of control over branded stock. Do not assume every small provider is unsuitable, but require the same verifiable receiving arrangement and written obligations regardless of size. Refuse unexplained substitutions of recipient or destination, and avoid releasing material merely because a truck is already at the gate and storage space is becoming inconvenient.",
