          "Assess how the provider controls people, locations and records throughout the job. Ask who identifies media, who can access it before treatment, where intermediate storage occurs and which subcontractors participate. Confirm whether requested supervision or on-site work is actually available and suitable for the premises. Request a redacted evidence format and a description of verification, validation and exception handling, then have qualified security personnel review the answers. Avoid supplying actual confidential files, account credentials or detailed sensitive system configurations to demonstrate the scope. The bidder normally needs enough metadata to assess the service, not access to the information whose protection is the purpose of the procurement.",
