          "Data treatment and environmental compliance address different obligations. A business sanitizing its own purchased office devices does not automatically become a producer under the e-waste rules. Importing covered products, marketing equipment under its own brand or conducting other regulated activities calls for a separate role assessment against current requirements. Confirm the relevant registered receiving arrangement for retired electronics and residual media, including any downstream organisation used by the sanitization provider. Assess batteries through their separate framework, particularly when equipment contains embedded or damaged packs requiring specialist handling. A destruction report is not an EPR target reconciliation, and environmental registration alone does not establish that the provider's media process meets security policy.",
