          "Put the agreed boundaries into the contract and site work plan. Define release authority, required site permissions, contractor coordination, custody transitions and the records supplied for each waste stream. Require approval for relevant changes in destination, subcontractors, treatment route or material classification. State how rejected equipment remains controlled and who pays for agreed additional assessment or revised logistics. Include confidentiality where production information or proprietary designs may be exposed during assessment. Separate service deliverables from statutory duties, which depend on actual roles, material classification and site requirements. A purchase order saying remove all electronics is too vague to establish safe engineering work, suitable environmental treatment and a defensible documentation trail.",
